{
  "_id": "romans3",
  "book": {
    "_id": "romans",
    "title": "Romans",
    "titleShort": "Rom.",
    "titleOfficial": "",
    "subtitle": "",
    "summary": "",
    "chapterDelineation": "Chapter"
  },
  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Romans",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 3,
    "summary": "Man is not justified by the law of Moses—He is justified through righteousness, which comes through faith in Christ, made possible through Christ’s atoning sacrifice.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "What advantage then hath the Jew? or what profit is there of circumcision?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 4,
            "text": "JST Rom. 3:1–2 What advantage then hath the Jew over the Gentile? or what profit of circumcision, who is not a Jew from the heart? But he who is a Jew from the heart, I say hath much every way …"
          },
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "GR preeminence."
          },
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 73,
            "text": "TG Circumcision."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 57
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Much every way: chiefly, because that unto them were committed the oracles of God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 74,
            "text": "Acts 7:38; 2 Ne. 29:4 (4–6)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For what if some did not believe? shall their unbelief make the faith of God without effect?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "1 Ne. 8:28 (26–28)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "God forbid: yea, let God be true, but every man a liar; as it is written, That thou mightest be justified in thy sayings, and mightest overcome when thou art judged.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "GR May it not be!"
          },
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "Alma 30:42 (37–42)."
          },
          {
            "start": 96,
            "end": 105,
            "text": "Ps. 51:4."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But if our unrighteousness commend the righteousness of God, what shall we say? Is God unrighteous who taketh vengeance? (I speak as a man)",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3,
            "text": "JST Rom. 3:5–8 (Appendix)."
          },
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 34,
            "text": "GR recommend."
          },
          {
            "start": 87,
            "end": 98,
            "text": "2 Ne. 26:7; Alma 42:1 (1, 13–25)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 82
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "God forbid: for then how shall God judge the world?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "GR May it not be!"
          },
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "TG Jesus Christ, Judge."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For if the truth of God hath more abounded through my lie unto his glory; why yet am I also judged as a sinner?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 50,
            "text": "GR in, by, because of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And not rather, (as we be slanderously reported, and as some affirm that we say,) Let us do evil, that good may come? whose damnation is just.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 124,
            "end": 133,
            "text": "TG Damnation."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 15
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "What then? are we better than they? No, in no wise: for we have before proved both Jews and Gentiles, that they are all under sin;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 35
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "As it is written, There is none righteous, no, not one:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 31,
            "text": "Ps. 14:2–3; 53:1 (1–3)."
          },
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 41,
            "text": "TG Man, Natural, Not Spiritually Reborn."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "There is none that understandeth, there is none that seeketh after God.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "They are all gone out of the way, they are together become unprofitable; there is none that doeth good, no, not one.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 32,
            "text": "D&C 82:6."
          },
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 71,
            "text": "Luke 17:10 (7–10); Mosiah 2:21 (20–21)."
          },
          {
            "start": 98,
            "end": 102,
            "text": "D&C 33:4; 35:12."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Their throat is an open sepulchre; with their tongues they have used deceit; the poison of asps is under their lips:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 6,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "Ps. 5:9."
          },
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 87,
            "text": "Ps. 140:3 (1–13)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 15
          },
          {
            "start": 96,
            "end": 98
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Whose mouth is full of cursing and bitterness:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 45,
            "text": "Alma 41:11; Morm. 8:31."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 14
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Their feet are swift to shed blood:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "Isa. 59:7 (7–8)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 14
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Destruction and misery are in their ways:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "Mosiah 3:25; Morm. 8:38."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 26
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And the way of peace have they not known:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "1 Ne. 20:22 (18–22)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "There is no fear of God before their eyes.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "D&C 10:56 (55–56)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Now we know that what things soever the law saith, it saith to them who are under the law: that every mouth may be stopped, and all the world may become guilty before God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 102,
            "end": 107,
            "text": "Ezek. 16:63."
          },
          {
            "start": 153,
            "end": 159,
            "text": "TG Guilt."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore by the deeds of the law there shall no flesh be justified in his sight: for by the law is the knowledge of sin.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "2 Ne. 25:23."
          },
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 33,
            "text": "TG Law of Moses."
          },
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 67,
            "text": "2 Ne. 2:5 (5–8)."
          },
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 88,
            "text": "GR through."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 97,
            "end": 99
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But now the righteousness of God without the law is manifested, being witnessed by the law and the prophets;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "TG God, the Standard of Righteousness."
          },
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "GR apart from, without intervention of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Even the righteousness of God which is by faith of Jesus Christ unto all and upon all them that believe: for there is no difference:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 38
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For all have sinned, and come short of the glory of God;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 19,
            "text": "Prov. 20:9; 1 Ne. 10:6. TG Man, Natural, Not Spiritually Reborn; Sin."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Being justified freely by his grace through the redemption that is in Christ Jesus:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5,
            "text": "JST Rom. 3:24 Therefore being justified only by his grace …"
          },
          {
            "start": 6,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "D&C 20:30."
          },
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "TG Grace."
          },
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 58,
            "text": "TG Jesus Christ, Redeemer."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Whom God hath set forth to be a propitiation through faith in his blood, to declare his righteousness for the remission of sins that are past, through the forbearance of God;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 23,
            "text": "GR purposed, designed beforehand."
          },
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 44,
            "text": "GR mercy seat. TG Jesus Christ, Atonement through; Redemption."
          },
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 71,
            "text": "TG Blood, Symbolism of."
          },
          {
            "start": 110,
            "end": 119,
            "text": "TG Remission of Sins."
          },
          {
            "start": 155,
            "end": 166,
            "text": "TG Forbear."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 29
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "To declare, I say, at this time his righteousness: that he might be just, and the justifier of him which believeth in Jesus.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 72,
            "text": "TG God, Justice of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 18
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Where is boasting then? It is excluded. By what law? of works? Nay: but by the law of faith.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 17,
            "text": "Alma 26:36 (10–12, 36); D&C 3:4; 84:73."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 6,
            "end": 8
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore we conclude that a man is justified by faith without the deeds of the law.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 45,
            "text": "TG Justification."
          },
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "TG Faith."
          },
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 62,
            "text": "GR apart from, without intervention of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Is he the God of the Jews only? is he not also of the Gentiles? Yes, of the Gentiles also:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "2 Ne. 30:2 (1–2)."
          },
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 84,
            "text": "TG Gentiles."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5
          },
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 37
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Seeing it is one God, which shall justify the circumcision by faith, and uncircumcision through faith.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "1 Tim. 2:5; D&C 121:28."
          },
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 58,
            "text": "TG Circumcision."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 12
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Do we then make void the law through faith? God forbid: yea, we establish the law.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "GR May it not be!"
          },
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 59,
            "text": "GR but."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
